body:
Pentest identified four security headers absent from all responses in both deployment modes (nginx/Docker and Node.js standalone).

## Changes

- **`Content-Security-Policy`** — locks resource loading to trusted origins: same-origin for scripts/API calls, `fonts.googleapis.com`/`fonts.gstatic.com` for Google Fonts, `images.pokemontcg.io`/`placehold.co` for card images, `media-src 'self'` for camera access
- **`Strict-Transport-Security`** — `max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains` (1 year, no `preload` — requires explicit domain registration)
- **`Permissions-Policy`** — `camera=(self)` (required for card scanning), all other sensitive features (`microphone`, `geolocation`, `payment`, `usb`) denied
- **`Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`** — isolates the browsing context against cross-origin attacks (e.g. Spectre)

## Approach

**`nginx.conf`** — four additional `add_header ... always` directives alongside the existing four.

**`server/index.mjs`** — single `applySecurityHeaders(res)` call at the top of `requestHandler` using `res.setHeader()`, ensuring all response paths (JSON, static files, SSE, image serving) carry the headers without duplicating them per route:

```js
const SECURITY_HEADERS = {
  'Content-Security-Policy': "default-src 'self'; ...",
  'Strict-Transport-Security': 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains',
  'Permissions-Policy': 'camera=(self), microphone=(), ...',
  'Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy': 'same-origin',
  // existing headers also consolidated here
}

function applySecurityHeaders(res) {
  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(SECURITY_HEADERS)) {
    res.setHeader(name, value)
  }
}
```
